+{
+  "task_id": "T24",
+  "repository": "wattclaw",
+  "mode": "demo",
+  "evidence": [
+    {
+      "path": "server/core/multi-tenant-gateway.js",
+      "symbol": "getHttpTargetForCurrentRequest",
+      "start_line": 448,
+      "end_line": 466,
+      "observation": "The per-request tenant router. It reads the request tenant from getRequestTenant() (or falls back to the requesting user's tenant / the default tenant), and returns { baseUrl: `http://${tenant.host}:${tenant.port}`, headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${tenant.token || ''}` }, tenant }. It only ever builds a target for the request's own context tenant and attaches that tenant's own token, which is exactly the allow path the demo replays: resolve the backend from the context tenant, then dispatch with its bearer credential."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "server/core/multi-tenant-gateway.js",
+      "symbol": "getHttpTargetForTenantId",
+      "start_line": 468,
+      "end_line": 485,
+      "observation": "Explicit-tenant target resolver. It looks the tenant up by id and throws `Tenant ${tenantId} not found` when the tenant does not exist, before ensureGatewayClient()/ensureConnected() are reached, so an unknown tenant produces no downstream dispatch. This is the deny boundary the demo mirrors for the unknown-tenant scenario (403 unknown_tenant, zero fake-backend hits)."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "server/core/multi-tenant-gateway.js",
+      "symbol": "callGatewayForTenant",
+      "start_line": 417,
+      "end_line": 426,
+      "observation": "Cross-tenant RPC entry point that resolves the tenant by id and throws `Tenant ${tenantId} not found` before ensureGatewayClient()/ensureConnected() and gateway.call(). It confirms rejection happens in-process before any dispatch when the requested tenant identity is not a known tenant."
